<title>UK: BOE GIVES UK MONEY MARKET 720 MLN STG FURTHER HELP.</title>
<headline>BOE GIVES UK MONEY MARKET 720 MLN STG FURTHER HELP.</headline>
<dateline>LONDON 1997-08-11</dateline>
<text>
<p>The Bank of England said it provided the UK money market with a further 720 million stg of assistance at established interest rates.</p>
<p>All 720 million pounds was allotted in repos to August 26, bringing the total liquidity provided by the Bank so far on Monday to 867 million.</p>
<p>It earlier forecast a money market shortage of 1.05 billion stg.</p>
<p>-- London Newsroom +44 171 542 7708</p>
